    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP on 2026-06-22 is headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (77.77) and **Brice Turang** (72.06), both of whom benefit significantly from the \"SB Hunter\" multiplier. **Corbin Carroll** is our highest-rated play, capitalizing on the slow delivery of Andre Pallante and a favorable platoon spot in the #3 hole. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (70.36) profiles as an elite play against Framber Valdez; his high score is bolstered by a massive 13% platoon edge and the opportunity to exploit a pitcher who historically struggles to control the run game. **James Wood** (66.45) remains a set-and-forget anchor, providing an elite floor thanks to his .402 xwOBA, regardless of opponent data availability.\n\nWhile **Kyle Karros** (60.60) narrowly squeezed into the UTIL spot due to a 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Jake Bennett, he represents the most volatile end of our active roster. The hardest bench decision involved **Gabriel Moreno** (58.16) and **Austin Riley** (57.74); both sit just shy of our \"Strong\" start threshold (60+). **Austin Riley** in particular was suppressed by a matchup against the high-strikeout Michael King and a defensive efficiency penalty, despite his talent profile. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Brice Turang**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **James Wood**, **Jose Caballero**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Kyle Karros** closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters introduces significant variance to our projected efficiency scores. \n\nWith **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined on the IL, and **Josh Naylor** and **Tyler Soderstrom** off the board due to schedule gaps, our depth is thin. We are maintaining a conservative approach with **Zach McKinstry** (45.53), who faces an uphill battle against Gerrit Cole; he remains active only to preserve our seasonal game caps, provided he cracks the starting lineup. Should **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Cole Young**, or **Carson Williams** see unexpected lineup changes, we are prepared to pivot, though current projections suggest our active unit provides the highest probability of closing the gap in stolen bases while maintaining our batting average floor.",
